# Trivy ignore list — accepted vulnerabilities ONLY.
#
# Policy (enforced by review, see docs/principal_engineer_review_report.md H-02):
#   1. One vulnerability ID (CVE/GHSA) per line.
#   2. Every entry MUST be justified in a trailing comment with:
#        - why it is accepted (no reachable path / mitigated / wontfix reason)
#        - an EXPIRY DATE after which the exception must be re-reviewed or fixed
#   3. Entries without justification + expiry will be rejected in review.
#   4. Re-run the scan at expiry: `trivy image --ignore-unfixed --severity CRITICAL,HIGH <image>`
#
# CI behavior: the scan FAILS the build on any fixable CRITICAL/HIGH finding
# that is not listed here (exit-code: 1 in .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# There are currently NO accepted exceptions — keep it that way if possible.
